Notice for data/gorilla_landmarks.npz
(written by scripts/fetch_datasets.py --gorilla on 2026-10-22T21:01:22Z)

The file holds the `gorf.dat` (30 female) and `gorm.dat` (29 male) gorilla skull
landmark arrays of the package (8 landmarks in 2-D per skull; data from Paul O'Higgins,
Hull-York Medical School; source: O'Higgins, P. & Dryden, I. L. (1993) Sexual dimorphism
in hominoids: further studies of craniofacial shape differences in Pan, Gorilla, Pongo,
Journal of Human Evolution 24:183-205).  R's 8 x 2 x n arrays were rearranged to
points (59, 8, 2) float64 (the 30 females first, then the 29 males, each in the
package's order) with labels 0 = female, 1 = male.  Values are unchanged.

The arrays were extracted from the source tarball of the R package "shapes"
version 1.2.8 by Ian L. Dryden (https://cran.r-project.org/package=shapes,
https://github.com/iandryden/shapes), which is distributed under the GNU
General Public License version 2 (GPL-2).  They are redistributed here under
the same licence, GPL-2, with this notice.  The full licence text is in
LICENSES/GPL-2.txt and at https://www.gnu.org/licenses/old-licenses/gpl-2.0.txt.
The GPL-2 applies to this data file; the rest of this repository is MIT-licensed
(see LICENSE).

Source tarball: shapes_1.2.8.tar.gz
